      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is the interface default, kept as the \"not supported\" path for managers that cannot honor reftable (in-memory, shared-refdb). Accepting `REFTABLE` here would silently create a FILES repository while reporting REFTABLE. `LocalDiskRepositoryManager` overrides this method and creates the reftable backend explicitly via `FileRepositoryBuilder.setRefStorageFormat(REFTABLE)`. So reftable creation is supported, by the override rather than the default.",
